{
  "about": "How each Traceveil check (C1-C10, NC) reads under several privacy laws. The checks are the same observations everywhere; only the cited provisions and the risk weight change. Severities are Traceveil's risk weighting for prioritising fixes, not a legal determination. `null` severity means the check has no direct counterpart in that law and is left out of that score. 'IN' uses the severities the app assigned (DPDP), so its score always equals the app's. Checks a profile does not list keep the app's severity and are marked unmapped. Inconclusive evidence (V0, or U1 naming trackers) makes every jurisdiction inconclusive.",
